1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,080
The Spare Part

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:14,359
Hey, what's going on?

3
00:00:14,859 --> 00:00:15,880
It was just working.

4
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:17,920
Hi there, Tom Thomas.

5
00:00:18,339 --> 00:00:19,300
Simka Nolik.

6
00:00:19,679 --> 00:00:20,660
Look, I've got a problem.

7
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:21,760
Sorry, no time to play.

8
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:22,780
We're busy.

9
00:00:23,039 --> 00:00:24,140
Busy? With what?

10
00:00:24,379 --> 00:00:26,300
We got put in charge here for the day.

11
00:00:26,879 --> 00:00:28,740
We even get to use one of the pack-o-mats.

12
00:00:28,739 --> 00:00:31,739
Papus and Masiya went out to visit our Fixie friends.

13
00:00:31,939 --> 00:00:35,100
Papus used to be with them at the Space Center years ago.

14
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:41,179
Ever since he was a boy, Papus dreamed of going into space.

15
00:00:41,259 --> 00:00:44,299
Then why not? Fixies work on rockets too!

16
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:47,219
He even got a job at the Astronaut Training Center.

17
00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:49,619
He was put in charge of the centrifuge,

18
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:52,140
and he made sure it worked perfectly.

19
00:00:52,219 --> 00:00:56,739
The centrifuge is a sort of very fast carousel for training astronauts.

20
00:00:56,740 --> 00:00:59,219
And Papus trained inside of it too!

21
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:03,579
Unfortunately, Papus never knew the rocket was scheduled to fly on his day off.

22
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:06,099
And when he found out, it was too late,

23
00:01:06,219 --> 00:01:08,740
and the rocket blasted off without him.

24
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:11,620
Since then, Papus hates his days off.

25
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:14,820
But he still longs to fix something like that centrifuge.

26
00:01:14,939 --> 00:01:18,180
You know, something turning around like a washing machine.

27
00:01:18,379 --> 00:01:23,300
Too bad for Papus that the one in his house seems to keep working perfectly fine.

28
00:01:23,299 --> 00:01:27,739
So that means today you fix everything?

29
00:01:28,739 --> 00:01:32,060
Uh-huh. Well then, it's your lucky day because my car just broke down.

30
00:01:32,179 --> 00:01:34,099
Hurrah! We've got work to do!

31
00:01:34,219 --> 00:01:35,819
Nolik, let's go!

32
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:43,179
Well, what broke down here?

33
00:01:43,379 --> 00:01:44,299
Wait a sec!

34
00:01:46,579 --> 00:01:48,539
Here! This part broke down.

35
00:01:48,659 --> 00:01:50,299
It's all covered in black!

36
00:01:50,379 --> 00:01:53,179
I wonder where we can get the same part but a clean one.

37
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:54,420
A clean one?

38
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:56,060
Nolik!

39
00:01:56,180 --> 00:01:57,180
Genius!

40
00:01:57,260 --> 00:01:59,460
There's the same exact part inside the dishwasher!

41
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:00,700
We can take it from there!

42
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:01,580
Come on!

43
00:02:13,340 --> 00:02:16,780
Do you have any idea how all these parts are connected to one another?

44
00:02:16,860 --> 00:02:18,500
With this thing right under you.

45
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:21,300
It's a special part called a circuit board.

46
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:26,500
A circuit board is made like this.

47
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:29,500
First, the board gets covered with a thin layer of metal.

48
00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:34,740
Then, paths are laid onto the board where the electricity is going to flow.

49
00:02:35,099 --> 00:02:40,060
After that, all of the extra metal is washed off of it with a special cleaning liquid,

50
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:43,340
leaving the metal paths that were drawn on the board.

51
00:02:44,340 --> 00:02:49,260
These paths work just like wires to connect the parts on the board to each other.

52
00:02:49,259 --> 00:02:53,459
And then all that's left to do is attach those parts to their places on the path.

53
00:02:56,979 --> 00:02:57,939
Pull it!

54
00:02:59,919 --> 00:03:00,519
Tideesh!

55
00:03:08,699 --> 00:03:10,699
Tom Thomas! Tideesh!

56
00:03:11,519 --> 00:03:13,399
Hooray! It works again!

57
00:03:14,539 --> 00:03:17,500
Tom Thomas, I'm about to start the dishwasher.

58
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:20,219
Are there any dirty dishes in your room?

59
00:03:20,780 --> 00:03:21,699
No.

60
00:03:22,219 --> 00:03:23,060
Slow down!

61
00:03:23,419 --> 00:03:24,460
Slow what down?

62
00:03:24,659 --> 00:03:25,860
Slow down your mom!

63
00:03:25,979 --> 00:03:28,699
We took the new part out of the dishwasher, see?

64
00:03:29,419 --> 00:03:31,979
Mom, wait! Don't start it!

65
00:03:32,419 --> 00:03:34,340
You need to put… put…

66
00:03:35,139 --> 00:03:37,740
Yeah, put in this one, uh, dirty cup.

67
00:03:37,819 --> 00:03:39,020
Nolik, follow me!

68
00:03:39,139 --> 00:03:41,099
Inside the TV is the same part!

69
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:51,300
Now back to the dishwasher.

70
00:03:55,460 --> 00:03:57,000
We barely made it.

71
00:03:57,639 --> 00:04:00,219
We grabbed the part from the TV in the living room.

72
00:04:00,759 --> 00:04:01,680
Not the TV.

73
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:04,659
Uh, my mom's favorite program is about to start.

74
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:15,039
The television is working now.

75
00:04:15,219 --> 00:04:16,639
And where did you get the part for it?

76
00:04:16,639 --> 00:04:18,759
From your dad's computer in his office!

77
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:21,519
Hi everybody! I'm home!

78
00:04:21,879 --> 00:04:23,759
Hi, hon! Are you ready for dinner?

79
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,039
In a bit. I've got to finish a little work on the computer.

80
00:04:27,319 --> 00:04:28,959
Simka, hurry!

81
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:31,319
Where else can we find that part?

82
00:04:31,439 --> 00:04:33,719
Stop! That's enough running!

83
00:04:34,519 --> 00:04:36,919
Here, take it back from the car.

84
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:42,959
And then we put the part back into the computer and it started working again!

85
00:04:43,039 --> 00:04:44,599
Oh, that was really silly!

86
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:49,800
Remember, you little experts, never repair any device at the cost of another one.

87
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:51,160
I understand now.

88
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:52,439
And I understand.

89
00:04:52,439 --> 00:04:56,600
If you were smart, you could have taken the part out of the old radio in the closet.

90
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:59,879
Papus, but you know the radio wouldn't work then.

91
00:04:59,879 --> 00:05:02,120
That old thing hasn't been working for years.

92
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:05,800
Masiya and I have pulled out half those parts already.

